userStories.description:
**Goal** — Restrict the advisory PRD scan to the specified provider-format patterns and emit at most one metadata-only warning per plan.

**Motivation** — One line per field (37 on one feature) teaches users to ignore the warning.

**Approach** — **Provider-format secret shapes, one summary line (`packages/nax/src/prd/secret-shapes.ts`, `packages/nax/src/plan/strategies/persist-prd.ts`).** `findPrdSecretShapes` no longer calls `redactSecrets`. It tests each story field (title, description, each acceptance criterion, in that order) against the `SECRET_VALUE_PATTERNS` entries whose `kind` is in a new exported constant:

```ts
export const PROVIDER_SECRET_KINDS: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set([
  "openai", "github", "github-pat", "npm", "aws", "gitlab", "google",
  "stripe", "slack", "telegram", "pem", "jwt",
]);
```

For each pattern it resets `re.lastIndex = 0` before testing. A field yields at most one finding, carrying the `kind` of the first matching pattern in `SECRET_VALUE_PATTERNS` order. `PrdSecretShape` gains `readonly kind: string`. The structured kinds (`assignment`, `bearer`, `basic`, `api-key-header`, `cookie`, `url-credentials`) and the redactor's structured key/value pass no longer produce findings. `_secretShapesDeps` (whose only member was `redactSecrets`) is deleted.

`finalizeAndWritePrd` (`persist-prd.ts`) replaces its one-warn-per-finding loop with at most one warn per plan:

```ts
getLogger().warn("plan", "PRD story text has secret shapes", {
  count: 3,
  fields: ["US-002 description", "US-004 title", "US-004 acceptanceCriteria[3]"],
  kinds: ["openai", "pem"],
});
```

`fields` lists `"<storyId> <field>"` in finding order. `kinds` holds the distinct kinds, sorted ascending. `count` equals `fields.length`. Nothing is logged when there are no findings. The existing `catch` that logs `PRD secret-shape scan could not run` stays as it is. The warning never carries the matched text.

**Scope** — In: modify the existing finder, finding type, and persistence warning loop; retain scope filtering and source text; update existing finder/advisory tests. The `toEqual` expectations in `packages/nax/test/unit/prd/secret-shapes.test.ts` gain `kind` (`"github"` for the `ghp_` value, `"openai"` for the `sk-` value). The advisory tests in `packages/nax/test/unit/plan/strategies/persist-prd-profile-log.test.ts` change from one `PRD story text has a secret shape` warn per field to one `PRD story text has secret shapes` warn per plan with `{ count, fields, kinds }`. Remove the `_secretShapesDeps` import and its redactor-throw test because the seam no longer exists; keep the `_persistPrdDeps.findPrdSecretShapes` throwing test. Out: run-report/view counts belong to US-001; story-metric success belongs to US-002. The log redactor (`redactSecrets`, `SECRET_VALUE_PATTERNS`) and its patterns are not changed; only the plan-time PRD scan narrows which kinds it reports. The plan secret-shape scan stays a warning; it never blocks `nax plan` or edits the PRD.

**Interface** —
```typescript
export interface PrdSecretShape {
  readonly storyId: string;
  readonly field: string;
  readonly kind: string;
}
findPrdSecretShapes(prd: PRD, scope?: ReadonlySet<string>): PrdSecretShape[]
```

The finder's signature is unchanged. Read `SECRET_VALUE_PATTERNS: readonly SecretValuePattern[]` and `SecretValuePattern { kind; re; acceptMatch? }`, imported from `@nathapp/nax-agent/internal` (the same entry `packages/nax/src/logger/index.ts:10` uses). Keep the existing `finalizeAndWritePrd(args: PersistPrdArgs): Promise<string>` signature and `_persistPrdDeps.findPrdSecretShapes` injection boundary. `PROVIDER_SECRET_KINDS` is exported from `secret-shapes.ts` and is exercised by this story's own tests; no new cross-story seam is needed.

**Failure handling** — `findPrdSecretShapes` throws inside `finalizeAndWritePrd`: One warn `PRD secret-shape scan could not run` with no data, and the PRD is still written (existing behaviour, kept). Never log the exception because it could contain candidate text.

**Testing** — Use three-session-tdd because this changes credential/token detection: the test writer changes tests only, the implementer changes production code without changing tests, and the verifier checks both. Demonstrate regressions with the specified synthetic key shapes, not real credentials. Assert structured-only negatives, provider positives including AWS/PEM, pattern-priority kind selection, scope, repeated-call stability, the exact allowlist, exact summary metadata, no matched text in warning data, silence for no findings, and output persistence after a thrown scan. Preserve existing scope/nonmutation and profile-log behavior; create no new files.
